Finding: {"title":"Weekly-outreach confirm endpoint inserts schedule events with zero conflict/capacity checking","severity":"HIGH","area":"Scheduling correctness / booking integrity","files":["src/server/routes/routes-ai-schedule.ts"],"detail":"POST /weekly-outreach/:runId/instructors/:instructorId/confirm (routes-ai-schedule.ts:3574-3683) reads `record.proposedScheduleJson.events` and inserts each into schedule_events in a plain for-loop (line 3621-3634) with NO double-booking check against existing events, NO instructor max-daily-hours check, NO operational-hours check, and no db.transaction wrapping the loop (unlike /publish and /publish-selected, which both use db.transaction and go through the constraint solver's isEntityFree/entityHoursOnDate guards). Any student/instructor/aircraft conflict already present, or introduced by two outreach runs confirmed concurrently, is inserted unchecked.","impact":"An instructor confirming their proposed weekly schedule can silently double-book themselves, a student, or an aircraft against events already on the live calendar (added since the proposal was generated) or against another outreach run confirmed around the same time. Because there's no transaction, a mid-loop failure also leaves a partial set of events committed with no rollback.","recommendation":"Route the proposed events through the same runScheduleSolver validation/insert path (or at minimum reuse isEntityFree-style occupancy checks against current schedule_events) before inserting, and wrap the insert loop in db.transaction like /publish and /publish-selected do.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

